# Line endings are not cosmetic for these files.
#
# `core.autocrlf=true` is set on Windows, so a checkout converts these to CRLF.
# MSYS2's bash then reads `set -euo pipefail\r` and dies on `$'\r': command not
# found`, and every line of a workflow's `run:` block reaches the runner with a
# trailing CR. The files are LF today only because nothing has re-checked them
# out since they were written; this pins LF so a checkout cannot break the build.
*.sh   text eol=lf
*.yml  text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
